}
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 452)</h2>
<p><b>⌘Z belongs to your markup again.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: ⌘Z could crash the app.</b> Undo was still the stock macOS one, aimed at the text-editing history the system quietly keeps as you type in a note or a text mark. Once that history referred to a field you'd already finished with, undoing it took the app down.</li>
<li><b>⌘Z now means "take back my last mark"</b> — every time, including after you've typed a note. Previously, typing anywhere in the app quietly hijacked ⌘Z away from your markup for the rest of the session.</li>
<li>Undo inside a text field still undoes your typing while you're editing it, and the text mark editor now keeps its own history that ends when the edit does.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
